## What we vendored

| Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `templates/semantic/` | PBIP/TMDL patterns (compat 1702, pbism 4.2, what-if GENERATESERIES) |
| `templates/report/` | PBIR `definition/` layout (version.json, pages/, report.json) |
| `templates/visuals/` | Selected `.github/pbi.kb` visualContainer JSON + a simple `tableEx` |
| `docs/tableau-dax-translation-guide.md` | DAX gotchas (compact-filter VAR hoist, LOD, parameters) |

## What we did **not** take

- Copilot CLI / agent orchestration
- Full example extracts, credentials, or migration-spec machinery
- Runtime dependency on the upstream Python package

BIEscape keeps its own AST parser (`engine/parser.py`) and formula transpiler
(`engine/transpiler.py`). Vendored files are **pattern templates** filled by
`engine/pbip/`.

## Patterns adopted from Franssens' worked examples (examples/superstore-sales-performance)

- PBIR shapes for lineChart / scatterChart wells, textbox (paragraphs + textRuns), shape (rectangle fill), pageNavigator
- Guidance that actionButton renders blank in Desktop (use shape), and that filledMap/map are deprecated in favor of azureMap
- visualContainer schema 2.9.0 (newest version that resolves)

## Ideas adopted from ionutsd/twbx_to_pbip (MIT, https://github.com/ionutsd/twbx_to_pbip)

No code was copied. We adopted the approach of choosing a visual from the mark class plus shelf contents (date axis -> line, dimension+measure -> bar/column, two measures -> scatter), mapping dashboard zones linearly onto a page, and recording each inference in a conversion report.
